Privacy Policy for Caller ID

GCaller ID provides caller identification and call-related features. This policy explains how we handle user and device data.

1. Data We Collect
- Phone-related data: incoming/outgoing call metadata needed for caller identification and call features.
- Contacts data: only if you grant Contacts permission, to show names and improve caller matching.
- Device/app data: app version, device model, OS version, diagnostics/crash logs.
- Optional user-provided data: any profile/support information you submit.

2. How We Use Data
- Provide caller identification and call functionality.
- Prevent abuse, fraud, and security issues.
- Improve app stability and performance.
- Respond to user support requests.

3. Data Sharing
We do not sell personal data.
We may share data with:
- Service providers (hosting, analytics, crash reporting) under contractual safeguards.
- Legal authorities when required by law.

4. Permissions
The app may request permissions such as Phone, Contacts, and Notifications only for app features described above. You can revoke permissions anytime in Android settings.

5. Data Retention
We retain data only as long as needed for service delivery, legal compliance, and security, then delete or anonymize it.

6. Data Security
We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards to protect data in transit and at rest.

7. Your Choices
You can:
- Deny or revoke permissions in device settings.
- Uninstall the app.
- Request account/data deletion (if applicable) by contacting us.

8. Children’s Privacy
The app is not directed to children under 13 (or local equivalent age).

9. Changes to This Policy
We may update this policy. Material changes will be posted with an updated effective date.

